1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,979
At the next stop, a router reads the label. Each router only knows the next step.

2
00:00:05,099 --> 00:00:07,467
If a road is busy, it sends it another way.

3
00:00:07,737 --> 00:00:10,510
Then the land ends. The cable goes into the sea.

4
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:13,361
From here, it all travels as light, under the sea.

5
00:00:13,631 --> 00:00:17,215
Three kilometres down, in the Arabian Sea, the photo is only light.

6
00:00:17,335 --> 00:00:21,388
Light in glass travels about 200,000 kilometres every second.

7
00:00:21,658 --> 00:00:25,882
As it fades, a repeater, every 60 to 100 kilometres, boosts it.

8
00:00:26,488 --> 00:00:29,432
The cable is thin, about as thick as a garden hose.

9
00:00:30,834 --> 00:00:34,311
Steel wires and plastic protect it from anchors and sea water.

10
00:00:35,286 --> 00:00:37,526
A copper tube carries power to the repeaters.

11
00:00:38,466 --> 00:00:40,877
In the middle, glass fibres, thin as a hair.
